The reference semantics explicitly supports whitespace `split`, string case conversion/counting, list append, and `for`, so I’m using those primitives. This keeps the implementation inside the translator’s subset and reduces the symbolic proof to one outer list traversal; consonant counting itself becomes a closed expression over each word.
